    slug: 'wyoming-pinnacle-powerful-solutions-elder-mail-scam',
    description: `Pinnacle Powerful Solutions, LLC, along with principals Linda Pearson and Ron Yung, mailed Wyoming consumers invitations offering a free steak dinner in exchange for sitting through a sales pitch for home energy-efficiency merchandise the company claimed could cut utility bills by up to 40%, while also falsely representing that the products were affiliated with NASA and served at well-known local steakhouses — claims the Wyoming Attorney General's Consumer Protection and Antitrust Unit found had no basis. The tactic specifically drew in elderly consumers, who make up a disproportionate share of fraud victims nationally in part because "free meal" sales events are marketed and timed to reach retirees with time to attend a weekday presentation. The office resolved the matter through a Consent Judgment barring Pinnacle Powerful Solutions, Pearson, and Yung from selling home-efficiency merchandise in Wyoming for five years, requiring full refunds to every Wyoming consumer who bought in — roughly $85,000 — and imposing $60,000 in suspended civil penalties that become due if the defendants violate the judgment's terms. Consumers invited to a "free" meal in exchange for a sales presentation should treat any claimed government, scientific, or brand affiliation as unverified until confirmed independently, get a written, itemized quote before committing to anything, and avoid signing a purchase agreement on the spot under the pressure of "limited time" seating or introductory pricing.`,
